The next example demonstrates using OpenWindowAndLink() instead of GetWindowByID() This introduce an interesting question: When to use OpenWindowAndLink()? If the parent window will call one object of the sub window then use OpenWindowAndLink() i.e. the relationship between the parent window and the sub window is one-to-one. If the parent window will call many objects of the sub window at different times Then use GetWindowByID() to determine which object to use i.e. the relationship between the parent window and the sub window is one-to-many. Screen Shot: 	:alt: Objects Library Example - Shot 4 

